# L §2.3 parse rule 6: "min(k in ks) is the aggregate, and count(k in a, j in b) binds two."
# count of two bindings over 2 and 3 keys: 2 × 3 = 6 binding tuples.  min of a bare binding over an
# index is its first key in index order (keys compare in index order, L §4.2).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

index a = [x, y]
index b = [p, q, r]

def n: int = count(i in a, j in b)
def lo: key b = min(j in b)

ask q1: n, lo
=== expect
q1: (6, p)
  cut 2026-01-01
